      "claim": "Verapamil, the closest structural analogue, shows complete human intestinal absorption (C190, C216), high Caco-2/MDR-MDCK permeability (C189, C193, C206, C225, C233, C220, C231), and human jejunal Peff >2e-4 cm/s (C235, C265).",
      "card_ids": ["C190","C216","C189","C193","C206","C225","C233","C220","C231","C235","C265"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 gut-wall efflux records show verapamil is a P-gp substrate; some assays show P-gp-sensitive permeability (C274), but high passive permeability and essentially complete in vivo intestinal absorption mean efflux does not determine F (C257, C251, C281, C238, C265); first-pass metabolism is the main F determinant (C264).",
      "card_ids": ["C274","C257","C251","C281","C238","C265","C264"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The query's low neutral fraction (0.02) is a physicochemical caveat, but verapamil-like high permeability and transferable F values >=20% support F>=20%; no affirmative evidence indicates F<20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C190","C216","C235","C265","C11","C28"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "gut_wall_efflux_intestinal_metabolism",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": [
        "C260","C263","C264","C265","C251","C254","C257","C281","C238","C242",
        "C277","C274","C280","C237","C252","C282","C247","C278","C283","C273"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule.",
    "No query-specific gut-wall efflux or intestinal metabolism data; L5 records are for verapamil and other reference molecules.",
    "First-pass hepatic metabolism for the query is not directly measured; verapamil's low F is attributed to first-pass metabolism (C264), but transferable F values remain >=20%.",
    "Low neutral fraction (0.02) due to basic pKa 9.05 may affect absorption, but verapamil-like high permeability suggests it is not limiting; no query-specific permeability data exist.",
    "No matched oral-versus-IV exposure data for the query are provided."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L5 verapamil-specific gut-wall efflux records confirm high intestinal permeability and essentially complete absorption despite P-gp efflux, with first-pass metabolism as the main F determinant; combined with L1/L2 direct F values >=20% for verapamil and valbenazine, prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

